Author: Dr. Thorsten Tepper Garcia

Created: 22 DEC 2024

About:

An attempt to port the outdated (pre 2024) ramses/patch/init/restart patch into the most recent one.

Despite my efforts, the patch does not work yet as expected.
In particular, when restarting a N-body/hydro simulations, the code runs out of memory, requiring to increase ngridmax to values beyond what is reasonable.
Pure N-body simulations work just fine.

I'll try to collaborare with some Ramses experts to identify the issue.

In the meantime, I've created a similar patch of my own that basically borrows (and modifies) the load_ramses subroutine from here with the dice patch (and my patched version); see patch/tepper/dice_restart. This patch works just fine.


These are the required files and their respective locations:
rsync -avzP ../../../amr/adaptive_loop.f90  .
rsync -avzP ../../../amr/init_refine.f90 .
rsync -avzP ../../../amr/init_time.f90 .
rsync -avzP ../../../hydro/init_flow_fine.f90 .
rsync -avzP ../../../pm/add_list.f90  .
rsync -avzP ../../../pm/init_part.f90 .
rsync -avzP ../../../pm/particle_tree.f90 .
rsync -avzP ../../../pm/rho_fine.f90 .

